    "https://clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt/system/files/assets/files/faculty-position-marketing-2026_1.pdf": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Quantitative Marketing",
      "description": "Deadline: October 1st, 2026  Palma de Cima, 1649-023 Lisboa Tel. +351 217 270 250 www.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt FACULTY POSITION IN QUANTITATIVE MARKETING Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics, Portugal Católica Lisbon School of Business and Economics (Católica-Lisbon SBE) invites applications for a full-time tenure- track Assistant Professor position in Quantitative Marketing, beginning in September 2027. We seek an outstanding scholar whose research and teaching will contribute to the next stage of the Marketing group's development and reinforce the School's position as one of Europe's leading research -oriented business schools. Applicants should have completed, or expect to complete, a PhD before the appointment date. A Strategic Opportunity The Marketing group at Católica-Lisbon SBE has established internationally recognized strengths in consumer behavior, branding, marketing communications, digital marketing, and consumer decision making. As marketing is being reshaped by advances in data, artificial intelligence, and digital techno logies, the School is making a strategic investment to expand its expertise in quantitative and technology-enabled marketing. The ideal candidate will play an important role in shaping this next phase of development. Beyond contributing to teaching, the new faculty member is expected to build an internationally visible research program and foster interdisciplinary collaboration across the School, particularly with colleagues in Operations & Data Science. Research Profile We welcome applications from candidates with proven research interests in one or more of the following areas: • Marketing Analytics and Customer Insights • Artificial Intelligence in Marketing • Marketing Technology (MarTech) • Customer Experience Analytics • Pricing and Revenue Management • Digital Platforms and Data-Driven Marketing We are interested in scholars addressing important marketing questions using rigorous empirical, econometric, computational, or machine -learning approaches. Outstanding candidates working in closely related areas of quantitative marketing are strongly encouraged to apply. What We Offer Católica-Lisbon SBE is a research-intensive institution that provides an environment designed to support ambitious scholarship. Faculty are expected to pursue research aimed at the leading journals in marketing and related disciplines. The School offers competitive compensation, substantial research support, funding for conferences and data acquisition, an active international seminar program, and teaching loads that allow substantial time for research. Faculty also benefit from extensive opportunities for collaboration across disciplines, a highly international academic community, and a collegial culture that values intellectual curiosity, research excellence, and innovation in teaching. Palma de Cima, 1649-023 Lisboa Tel. +351 217 270 250 www.clsbe.lisboa.ucp.pt Candidate Qualifications Applicants for the Assistant Professor position should demonstrate outstanding potential for publishing in top -tier journals. Candidates at more senior levels should have an established record of high -quality publications in top journals in marketing or a closely related field, excellence in teaching, and the ability to strengthen the research profile of the Marketing group. We seek scholars who combine substantive marketing insight with methodological rigor. Proven experience with analytical and computational tools (e.g., R, Python, SQL, Julia, Stata, or similar) is important. We particularly value candidates who actively contribute to a vibrant academic community through collaboration, intellectual engagement, and collegiality, and who are enthusiastic about participating in the day -to-day life of the department, including regular on-campus interaction with colleagues, doctoral students, and students. The Marketing Group The Marketing group consists of internationally trained faculty with publications in leading journals including the Journal of Marketing, Journal of Marketing Research, Journal of Consumer Research, Journal of Consumer Psychology, Marketing Science, and other premier outlets. The group combines a collaborative culture with ambitious research goals and is committed to developing internationally recognized scholarship while delivering outstanding teaching across undergraduate, master's, MBA, and executive education programs. This appointment reflects the group's long -term vision of broadening its expertise in quantitative and technology - enabled marketing while building on its established strengths in behavioral research. About Católica-Lisbon SBE CATÓLICA-LISBON is consistently ranked among Europe's leading business schools and holds the prestigious triple accreditation (AACSB, EQUIS and AMBA). The School's programs are taught entirely in English and attract students and faculty from around the wor ld. Faculty are affiliated with CUBE, one of Portugal's leading research centers in economics and management, providing an excellent platform for interdisciplinary research and international collaboration. Located in Lisbon, one of Europe's most vibrant ca pitals, Católica-Lisbon SBE offers an exceptional quality of life together with a dynamic international academic environment. Application Procedure Applications should include: • Cover letter • Curriculum vitae • Research statement • Teaching statement • Job market paper or representative publications • Three letters of recommendation (for junior candidates) Priority consideration will be given to applications received by October 1st. Applications will remain open until the position is filled. Initial interviews will be conducted online, followed by campus visits for shortlisted candidates. For further information, please contact the Faculty Recruitment Office and the Chair of the Search Committee. Applications should be submitted to the Faculty Recruitment Office (internationalrecruit.clsbe@ucp.pt). Any questions regarding the position may be directed to Prof. Daniel Fernandes (daniel.fernandes@ucp.pt). "
    }
